rted from stamped), it doesn't matter. I'll leave as `job_copy`.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: `tool_built_job` runs `run(\"pin\", ...)` which requires the maker log to be ABSENT (pin refused if seat's log has a call). It does `mlog.unlink()` before pin and restores after. On FIX, maker log is `harness-maker-fixture.log`. Fine.\n\nNow the T4 block after tool_built_job:\n```python\nTJ = tool_built_job(\"tool-built\")\n...\nrc, out = emit(TJ, o, allow_hand=False)\n```\nFine.\n\nNow E2:\n```python\nj = job_copy_logged(\"t2-pass-at\")\n```\n\u2192 `emitted_copy(\"t2-pass-at\")`.\n\nAnd the 59s:\n```python\nj = job_copy_logged(\"tol-59\")\n```\n\u2192 `emitted_copy(\"tol-59\")`.\n\nAnd tol-61:\n```python\nj = job_copy_raw(\"tol-61\")\n```\n\u2192 `job_copy(\"tol-61\")` (now FIX unstamped).\n\nNow, all `job_copy(...)` \u2192 `emitted_copy(...)`. That's a lot of blocks. I need unique SEARCH context for each. Since many calls look similar (`j = job_copy(\"...\")`), I can include the fixture name which is unique.\n\nLet me be careful: some `job_copy(...)` appear inside `refused(..., job_copy(...), ...)`. And some inside loops.\n\nLet me now systematically list every occurrence with its line context from the file:\n\n1. `job_copy(\"given\")`:\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"given\")\np = json.loads((j / \"packet.json\").read_text()); p[\"disposition_state\"] = \"given\"\n```\n\n2. `job_copy(\"no-disposition\")`:\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"no-disposition\")\np = json.loads((j / \"packet.json\").read_text()); p.pop(\"disposition_state\")\n```\n\n3. `job_copy(\"bad-remedy\")`:\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"bad-remedy\")\nc = json.loads((j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").read_text()); c[\"violations\"][\"V1\"][\"remedy\"][\"text\"] = \"a remedy nobody wrote\"\n```\n\n4. `job_copy(\"no-violation-dimension\")`:\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"no-violation-dimension\")\nc = json.loads((j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").read_text()); c[\"violations\"][\"V1\"].pop(\"dimension\")\n```\n\n5. `job_copy(\"same-family\")`:\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"same-family\")\n```\n\n6. `job_copy(\"no-inputs\")`:\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"no-inputs\")\n(j / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\").unlink()\n```\n\n7. `job_copy(\"open-job\")`:\n```python\nj = job_copy(\"open-job\")\np = json.loads((j / \"packet.json\").read_text()); p.pop(\"terminal_state\")\n```\n\n8. failure loop:\n```python\nfor ov, tag in ((\"hand-times\", \"time\"), (\"after-emit\", \"after-emit\"), (\"router-endpoint\", \"endpoint\"),\n                (\"agent-approval\", \"approval\")):\n    refused(f\"failure fixture {ov}\", job_copy(f\"fail-{ov}\", ov), tag)\n```\n\n9. `out_ = refused(\"hand times typed after the maker call also break event order\", job_copy(\"fail-order\", \"hand-times\"), \"order\")`\n\n10. `j = job_copy(\"keep-old\", \"agent-approval\"); keep = TMP / \"keep-old.json\"; keep.write_text(\"OLD RECORD\\n\")`\n\n11. `j = job_copy_raw(\"tol-61\")` \u2192 `job_copy(\"tol-61\")`\n\n12. `j = job_copy_logged(\"tol-59\")` \u2192 `emitted_copy(\"tol-59\")`\n\n13. `j = job_copy(\"vendor-host\")`\n\n14. `o = refused(\"pinned provider, another provider served the call (fallback)\", job_copy(\"pin-fb\", \"pin-fallback\"), \"endpoint\")`\n\n15. `o = refused(\"pinned provider, the log does not say who served the call\", job_copy(\"pin-miss\", \"pin-provider-missing\"), \"endpoint\")`\n\n16. `refused(\"a pin declared after the seat's first call\", job_copy(\"pin-late\", \"pin-late\"), \"order\")`\n\n17. `j = job_copy(\"pin-attempt\")`\n\n18. `j = job_copy(\"pin-none\"); (j / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").unlink(); ledger_edit(j, lambda c: c.pop(\"routing\"))`\n\n19. `j = job_copy(\"pin-unlogged\"); (j / \"inputs\" / \"custody-events.jsonl\").unlink()`\n\n20. `j = job_copy(\"pin-unpinned\", \"routing-unpinned\")`\n\n21. `j = job_copy(\"pin-deny\")`\n\n22. `j = job_copy(\"pin-nobody\")`\n\n23. `j = job_copy(\"ledger-pin-late\")`\n\n24. `j = job_copy(\"ledger-pin-ok\"); (j / \"custody\" / \"evidenc