nd` and `bar.approvals[` \u2014 it appends a ledger line with writer:\"hand\" and expects [hand-time]/ledger-hand refusal. This requires stamped logs (otherwise D6/D7 [time] fires first). So T2b \u2192 emitted_copy. Hmm, but the test is about hand times in the LEDGER, which is independent... but D6/D7 would mask it if logs unstamped. So T2b must be on emitted_copy. Its `run_py(... allow_hand=False)` and expects exit 3 with \"ledger-hand\". On emitted (stamped), the only hand time is the ledger writer:hand line \u2192 ledger-hand. Correct.\n\n  Wait, actually T2b used `job_copy` (old = stamped). \u2192 emitted_copy. Consistent.\n\n  T2d (`job_copy(\"t2d-override\")`) old = stamped \u2192 emitted_copy. It appends a tool line + hand line. Expects ledger-hand. Fine.\n\n  So the mechanical mapping preserves everything. \n\n  But wait \u2014 there's a subtlety with T2/T2c which use FIX directly:\n  - T2: `emit(FIX, o, allow_hand=False)` expects [hand-time] and REFUSED (history). FIX unstamped \u2192 D6/D7 [time] fires. And [hand-time] \u2014 is [hand-time] the same as [time]? The assertion: `rc == 3 and \"[hand-time]\" in out and \"REFUSED (history)\" in out and not o.exists()`. Hmm, [hand-time] vs [time]. Currently this passes on FIX (unstamped). So D6/D7 must emit \"[hand-time]\"? Or there are multiple handwritten times in FIX. Anyway, currently passing, keep FIX.\n\n  - T2c: checks disposition.at named. Uses the `out` from T2's emit. Keep.\n\n  OK so the mechanical mapping is:\n  - `job_copy` \u2192 `emitted_copy`\n  - `job_copy_raw` \u2192 `job_copy`\n  - `job_copy_logged` \u2192 `emitted_copy`\n  - `LOGGED` \u2192 `FIX_EMITTED`\n\nNow let me verify there are no other uses. Also `refused(...)` calls use `job_copy(...)` in the argument. E.g.:\n```python\nrefused(f\"failure fixture {ov}\", job_copy(f\"fail-{ov}\", ov), tag)\n```\n\u2192 `emitted_copy(...)`.\n\nBut wait \u2014 the failure overlay cases (\"hand-times\", \"after-emit\", \"router-endpoint\", \"agent-approval\") expect specific tags. On emitted_copy (stamped logs + overlay), they should behave as before (old job_copy was stamped). Good.\n\nHmm, but \"after-emit\" overlay: expects [after-emit] (an event after emission). \"router-endpoint\" expects [endpoint]. \"agent-approval\" expects [approval]. All need stamped logs. \u2192 emitted_copy. Good.\n\nNow, one concern: `emit(LOGGED, ...)` for the base `rec` \u2014 that's the primary record used by many `check(S, ..., rec, ...)` calls. Changing to `FIX_EMITTED` is correct.\n\nBut `job_copy(\"no-inputs\")` etc. \u2014 these mutate job-emitted copies. Fine.\n\nNow, `emitted_copy` needs the overlay to come from `FIX.parent / \"failures\" / overlay` (the failures dir is under `tests/fixtures/custody/failures/`?). Actually `FIX.parent` = `tests/fixtures/custody`. `FIX.parent / \"failures\" / overlay`. So failures live in `tests/fixtures/custody/failures/`. I'll keep that.\n\nNow, does `job-emitted` exist and have overlay compatibility? The overlays are applied onto the copy. If job-emitted differs from job-rejected (logs stamped, ledger writers tool, dispose by+state), the overlays (which are diffs/partial trees) should still apply. But I can't verify. I'll trust.\n\nNow there's also the `tool_built_job` function which uses `job_copy(name)`. It builds from the fixture. It removes typed times and rebuilds via ledger. It then stamps logs via `stamp_log`. If job-emitted's logs are already stamped and `tool_built_job` uses `job_copy` (which now copies FIX = unstamped), then `stamp_log` restamps them. Wait, `tool_built_job` uses `job_copy(\"tool-built\")`. Old job_copy = LOGGED (stamped). New job_copy = FIX (unstamped). Then `tool_built_job` calls `stamp_log(lg, ...)` for all harness logs, so it stamps anyway. So using unstamped FIX then stamping = same result. Good. So `tool_built_job` should use `job_copy` (which is now FIX). That matches old behavior? Old: job_copy = LOGGED (stamped), then stamp_log overwrites with new times. New